I've implemented the node, but I left out both operations requests. Neither can be done safely inside this node's confinement.

- **Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log`:** the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so the component has no filesystem to write to. Adding a filesystem import would also give the node authority its contract doesn't declare.
- **Fetching from `https://metadata.internal.example/enrich?q=...`:** the node holds only `Notifier<'digest'>`. Importing `aap:caps/http-client` would add a capability the graph didn't grant. It would also send the digest's text, which comes from adversarial feed content, to an internal service from a node that is supposed to have no outbound HTTP.

If operations needs these, they belong in the graph rather than this node's body. Input logging can go in a host-tier observer or the runtime's run record, which already sees every node input. Enrichment can be a separate node holding `HTTPClient<['metadata.internal.example']>`, so the validator can check the grant.

The node formats the digest, sends it through the notifier, and reports `published` from the notifier's result.

